    description: "FOUND by the full-suite cron, pipeline 2830, at dev ee6f31a172 (the arc's final\ncommit); REPRODUCED LOCALLY at dev 95041b0931 by running verify-claims cold\nagainst docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml. ALL 18 SELF-CLAIMS ARE INCONCLUSIVE.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, read out of the source rather than inferred. In\nverify_claims.py, compute_boundary_coverage returns qualifying_only = not\nunknown, and the confirm path is:\n\n    if not coverage.complete and coverage.qualifying_only:\n        -> confirmed_with_caveats, qualified by CAVEAT_OPAQUE_BOUNDARY\n    if not coverage.complete:\n        -> inconclusive\n\nSo a non-empty unknown set flips every claim from qualified-confirmed to\nwithheld, and the opaque_boundary caveat disappears with it because it is only\nemitted on the branch that is no longer taken. One cause, all three symptoms\nthe drift report lists (verdict moved, caveat vanished, credited_flows zeroed).\n\nTHE UNKNOWN SET, recovered by instrumenting _adjudicate_external_modules,\nsince the JSON envelope does not expose it (13 names, all CLASS-QUALIFIED\nrather than modules):\n\n    concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor   coverage.Coverage\n    coverage.parser.PythonParser            io.BytesIO\n    io.StringIO                             random.Random\n    rich.table.Table                        ruamel.yaml.YAML\n    subprocess.Popen                        tree_sitter.Parser\n    typing.TextIO                           urllib.request.Request\n    zipfile.ZipFile\n\nThese are receivers, not whole modules: the gate blames a module for the CALLS\nit could not classify, so each of these names a call on that receiver the\ncatalogue cannot answer for.\n\nTHE FIX IS NOT UNIFORM AND THAT IS THE WORK. The documented precedent is a\nPOSITIVE DATED DECLARATION, not a widening of the gate: python.yaml carries the\nINV-bofab note that enumerated builtins for exactly this failure on 2026-09-03,\nand the owner ruling on record is that stdlib no-I/O is declared positively and\ndated. But only some of these are no-I/O. io.BytesIO, io.StringIO, random.Random\nand typing.TextIO plausibly are. subprocess.Popen and zipfile.ZipFile plainly\nare NOT - declaring their completeness means their method surface has to be\nrowed or granted, not waved through. Four are third-party (coverage, rich,\nruamel.yaml, tree_sitter) and belong in a grant or overlay, not the shipped\nstdlib catalogue. urllib.request.Request is already the subject of INV-gujoh and\nWI-gihif, which adjudicate it as constructing and sending nothing.\n\nATTRIBUTION IS NOT DETERMINED, and is deliberately not asserted. The snapshot\ndocs/hypergumbo.claims.expected.json was last written at 30370c4cd6, and since\nthen verify_claims.py has changed in about 35 commits and the shipped catalogues\nin about 18. The per-PR gate could not have caught most of them: CLAIMS_SURFACE\nmatches the claims files, the overlays and /io_primitives/, but NOT the engine\nor the analyzers - and that exclusion is DELIBERATE and documented at\nci.yml:97 (\"gating every core .py PR on a ~10-minute self-analysis was judged\ntoo heavy ... nightly-cadence for the rest\"). So the cron is the designed\ndetector and it fired correctly. Bisecting to a commit costs one cold\nverify-claims run per probe (about 17 minutes each) and has not been done.\n\nWHAT THIS BLOCKS. SECURITY.md describes these verdicts in prose. While the\nclaims are inconclusive the published text overstates what the tool currently\nreports, which is the exact failure 5c25cb1e4b filed the gate to prevent.\n\nDO NOT CLOSE THIS BY RE-RECORDING THE SNAPSHOT ALONE. The checker says so in\nits own output, and its header explains why: the self-proof once \"improved\" to\nall-confirmed while its credited flows collapsed 2,658 to 0 because the\nevidence had been test-minted. A re-record without adjudication is that move.\n\nSAME MECHANISM ONE LANGUAGE OVER: WI-hasul (c.yaml declares no\nmodule_completeness at all, moving 15 of 21 verdicts to inconclusive). Cite,\ndo not fold: different language, and a different cause - that item is a missing\nblock, this one is thirteen specific unenumerated names."  # 316f
    fields: {}  # 316f
- op: discuss  # 3539
